<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sari Gelin</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sarı Gəlin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sari Gelin (Azerbaijani Sarı Gəlin), Sari Aghjik in Armenian and Dâman Kešân in Persian, is the name of a number of folk songs popular among the people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a>, above all present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>, and eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>. All versions use the same melody in the Bayati makam or mode but are sung with different words, and the country of its origin is contested.</p></div>
